*An {{Epic}} or {{Legendary}} {{Item|Wolf Pet}} is especially useful to tank oncoming attacks better, as its {{AN|Alpha Dog}} ability can cut down up to {{Green|30%}} of the damage received from the '''Sven Packmaster'''.
**Its {{AN|Pack Leader}} ability also increases the [[player]]'s {{Stat|Crit Damage}}, which stacks well with {{Item|Mastiff Armor}}'s {{AN|Absolute Unit}} ability, which gives more {{stat|hp}} per {{Stat|Crit Damage}}.
**Giving the pet a {{Item|Dwarf Turtle Shelmet}} can be a good idea if the player has a hard time fighting the boss due to being constantly thrown around by its high knockback.
**The extra {{stat|hp}} from this ability combo helps tank the pups that the '''Sven Packmaster''' {{SlayerTier|III}} and above spawns.
*'''Sven Packmasters''' {{SlayerTier|III}} and above will stop regenerating {{stat|hp}} once it starts spawning its pups, and the boss itself will move very slowly. It is recommended to heal oneself during this time try to not to take any {{stat|dmg}} when it is this state.<!--
**While it is spawning the pups, it becomes invulnerable to {{stat|dmg}} and becomes stationary.
**It will start regenerating and becomes agile again once all pups have died.-->
*A common strategy for players who cannot tank the '''Sven Packmaster'''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s attacks well is to fight it in water, which allows the player to control the damage they receive to prevent health regeneration. The pups that spawn with a '''Sven Packmaster''' {{SlayerTier|III}} and above will stop attacking the [[player]] and drown.
**The pond next in the {{zone|Mountain}}, near the {{zone|Ruins}} is quick and easy to fight the boss in<!--, but the surrounding [[Wolf]] in the area may be troublesome to players unless they acquire an [[Intimidation Artifact]]. The small size of the pond may not be suitable for players who are not used to the pups that will spawn on higher levels.-->. The [[player]] can grind out wolves that grant high amounts of XP in the {{zone|Howling Cave}} and then teleport to the {{zone|Ruins}} when there is little XP required to spawn the boss. A {{Item|Lead}} can be used on a [[Wolf]] to bring it to the pond, where the player kill it and spawn the boss.
*A {{Item|Radiant Power Orb}} and its upgrades are recommended for players using {{Item|Mastiff Armor}} to combat the '''Sven Packmaster'''.
**Normal, non-multiplicative regeneration items such as {{Item|Wand of Healing}} and its upgrades become next to useless when using {{Item|Mastiff Armor}} due to it barely adding up to the massive health pool it provides. Thus, a {{Item|Zombie Sword}} and its upgrade, the {{Item|Ornate Zombie Sword}} is a substitute for instant healing.
*Letting the boss hit the [[player]] every <15 seconds prevents the boss from regenerating. 
* Since the boss does {{stat|tdmg}} at higher tiers, which makes {{stat|def}} less valuable, armor that grants high amounts of {{stat|hp}}, like {{ID|Superior Dragon Armor]}}, are highly recommended to absorb the blows from the Packmaster. It is also a good idea to enchant armor with {{Ench|Growth}}, for an extra {{stat|hp}} boost.
**{{Ench|True Protection}} can help slightly in cutting down received {{stat|dmg}} from the '''Sven Packmaster'''.
*{{Stat|True Defense}} can be a bit of a liability to get in meaningful quantities early on, but good sources include
**{{Item|Wolf Pet}} for {{Stat|True Defense|+10}}, or if you are really desperate for more, the {{Item|Mithril Golem Pet}} for {{Stat|True Defense|+50}} 
**{{Item|God Potion}} will grant {{Stat|True Defense|+20}}
**A {{Item|Dwarf Turtle Shelmet}} grants {{Stat|True Defense|+10}}
**The {{Ench|True Protection}} enchantment grants {{Stat|True Defense|+5}}<!--|-
|
* There exists a bug that can cause the boss to run away from the player and gets stuck in a 1-block stair shortly after.
** This usually happens when the boss is too far away from its spawn point. Thus, it is best for you to plan out where to spawn the boss and not prematurely spawn it.
** It becomes impossible to kill it on {{SlayerTier|III}}+ due to its regeneration ability, unless you can miraculously beat its regeneration speed.
** If this happens it is best to simply cancel the slayer quest and start over.-->
*Wearing {{Item|Sorrow Armor}} is advised when fighting this boss, since it has enough {{Stat|True Defense}} to keep the [[player]] alive and additional {{Stat|Magic Find}}, helping the chances of dropping rarer loot.
*A {{Item|Souls Rebound}} used to be able to prevent the '''Sven Packmaster''' second phase from occurring and could kill it in one hit with decent gear. This method is no longer available as it has since been patched.

